      "id": "w5h5o6n",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Important Rules"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Never use 'will', 'shall', or 'would' inside the conditional ('if') clause itself.",
        "'Unless' inherently carries a negative meaning, so do not use 'not' in the clause attached to 'unless'.",
        "For hypothetical/unreal conditions in the second conditional, use 'were' for all subjects (e.g., 'If I were you...').",
        "In Third Conditional, verify the pairing: 'If + had + V3' must always take 'would have / could have + V3' in the main clause."
      ],
      "id": "n7yf0xp"
    },
